course: dictionary
lesson: 1147
title: Brie and debris
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Brie is a noun. It is the name of a soft, creamy cheese from France, with a white, soft rind, which is the skin on the outside. People often eat brie with bread or crackers at parties and picnics.
explain: Brie can also be a name. Brie is a region of France near Paris. When you see it with a capital letter, look at the words around it to decide whether it means the cheese or the place.
explain: «"De-brie" sounds like "debris", the broken bits left after something breaks; brie is a soft French cheese.» Debris and brie sound alike, but they mean different things. Debris is broken pieces, like the bits of a smashed plate. Brie is the cheese. Always check the meaning in the sentence.
fact: Brie is a noun, and it is uncountable, so you say some brie, not a brie.
fact: «Brie» means a soft, creamy French cheese with a white, soft rind.
fact: Brie comes from the Brie region near Paris, and «Brie» is also the name of that region of France.
fact: In French lessons, brie is one of many famous cheeses, such as camembert and roquefort.
fact: «Debris» means broken bits left after something breaks. It sounds like «brie», but it is spelled and used differently.
exercise: Which word means a soft, creamy French cheese? | *Brie | Region | Debris | Rind
exercise: «"De-brie" sounds like "debris", the broken bits left after something breaks.» What does debris mean? | *Broken bits left after something breaks | Soft, creamy cheese | The white skin on a cheese | A region of France near Paris
exercise: «We ate brie and crackers at the picnic.» Brie is a | Car | Dance | Broken piece of plate | *Soft cheese
test: Which sentence uses brie correctly? | We bought a brie for the picnic. | *We bought some brie for the picnic. | We bought bries for the picnic.
test: Brie is also the name of a region of France. Which city is it near? | *Paris | Marseille | London | Lyon
exam: Which word sounds like brie but means broken bits left after something breaks? | Cheese | Region | *Debris | Rind
